NOTE: crash-type poison message caused a genuine infinite crash-restart loop (7+ redeliveries observed) since the message is never acked - a real, distinct failure mode from R7-03's safe nack-based poison handling. Clearing queue before WITH-idempotency test.
=== real lesson found: purge doesn't clear unacked/in-flight messages ===
dup-order-A's crash-message kept redelivering after an earlier 'purge' because
it was always mid-delivery (unacked) at purge time - RabbitMQ purge only
removes messages in 'ready' state, not ones currently out for delivery.
Fix: drain it with an actual ack (not requeue) via the Management API get endpoint.
